---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import pulse from "../assets/pulse-001.png";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const dmg =
	"https://github.com/summerhammer/yellowhammer/releases/latest/download/Yellowhammer.dmg";
const repo = "https://github.com/summerhammer/yellowhammer";
---

<Layout
	title="Yellowhammer"
	description="Yellowhammer runs an unattended engineering Night for each of your Projects, on top of Orca ADE. It never writes a line of code and never merges to main."
>
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pb-16 sm:px-6">
		<header class="py-6">
			<span class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight">Yellowhammer</span>
		</header>

		<main>
			<section class="pt-10 pb-16 sm:pt-16" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
				<img
					src="/yellowhammer-mark.svg"
					alt="The Yellowhammer mark, a yellow bird in profile."
					width="112"
					height="112"
					class="mark-glow mb-8 size-24 sm:size-28"
				/>
				<h1 id="hero-title" class="text-4xl leading-tight font-bold tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-5xl">
					Go to bed with a specification. Wake up with pull requests.
				</h1>
				<p class="mt-6 max-w-[60ch] text-xl c-muted">
					Yellowhammer runs an unattended engineering Night for each of your Projects, on top of Orca ADE.
				</p>
				<div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-4">
					<a href={dmg} class="btn btn-primary">Download for Mac</a>
					<a href={repo} class="btn btn-secondary">Star on GitHub</a>
				</div>
				<p class="mt-4 text-sm c-muted">Requires macOS 26. Open source, MIT licence.</p>
				<p class="mt-10 max-w-[70ch] c-muted">
					It takes intent from a Linear board and authors the work itself when the board is empty. It routes each
					Work Card to an agent CLI, runs it in a Worktree, and opens one pull request per repository. It verifies
					the result against a Definition of Done written before any code existed, and reports back to the board.
					You read the result in the morning.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="night-title" class="pb-20">
				<h2 id="night-title" class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-balance">One Night, in order</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 max-w-[60ch] c-muted">
					A Night runs without you. This is one Night for one Project, told from evening to morning. The times are
					an example, and each Project sets its own schedule.
				</p>

				<ol class="timeline mt-12">
					<li class="stage">
						<p class="mono text-sm c-faint">Evening &middot; 22:00, for example</p>
						<h3 class="mt-1 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance">The board gets a plan.</h3>
						<p class="mt-2"><span class="act-label">author Act</span></p>
						<div class="mt-4 max-w-[65ch] space-y-3 c-muted">
							<p>
								The author Act selects one <span class="term">Feature</span> from your specification. It works out
								which repositories the Feature touches. It writes a flat set of <span class="term">Work Cards</span>,
								each for one repository, with an Architectural Brief on each.
							</p>
							<p>
								Every clause of the <span class="term">Definition of Done</span> cites a place in the specification.
								The clauses are written before any code exists.
							</p>
							<p>
								An empty board is a valid start. A specification too thin to cite stops here: the Feature goes
								<span class="term">Waiting on You</span> before any dispatch, and names the clauses it cannot cite.
							</p>
							<p>
								The first Act of the Night also opens the Night Card. A Night that stops at 02:00 still leaves it.
							</p>
						</div>
					</li>

					<li class="stage">
						<p class="mono text-sm c-faint">Deep night &middot; 02:00, for example</p>
						<h3 class="mt-1 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance">
							Agent CLIs write the code. Yellowhammer judges.
						</h3>
						<p class="mt-2"><span class="act-label">build Act</span></p>
						<div class="mt-4 max-w-[65ch] space-y-3 c-muted">
							<p>
								The build Act fires repeatedly through the Night. It routes each Work Card to an agent CLI,
								chosen by its Work Kind and its repository's role.
							</p>
							<p>
								Each repository gets one <span class="term">Repo Lane</span> in its own
								<span class="term">Worktree</span>, created by Orca ADE. Lanes run in parallel. Within a lane,
								Work Cards run one at a time, each through an architect, a worker and a reviewer.
							</p>
							<p>
								Yellowhammer runs your repository's Check itself before a reviewer sees any diff. A reviewer asking
								for changes is a Round. Each dispatch of a Work Card to a route is an Attempt.
							</p>
							<p>
								Both are bounded. When a <span class="term">Bound</span> is reached, work stops and says why. The
								Work Card becomes Blocked, with a Block Reason, or Waiting on You, with a question. The lane runs on
								past it.
							</p>
						</div>
					</li>

					<li class="stage">
						<p class="mono text-sm c-faint">Early morning &middot; 05:30, for example</p>
						<h3 class="mt-1 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance">
							One pull request per repository. No merge.
						</h3>
						<p class="mt-2"><span class="act-label">land Act</span></p>
						<div class="mt-4 max-w-[65ch] space-y-3 c-muted">
							<p>
								The land Act fires when the Feature's Work Cards are all finished. It test-merges each Feature Branch
								against its repository's mainline and pushes it.
							</p>
							<p>
								Then a different agent verifies the Definition of Done, clause by clause, against the specification.
								That agent's route differs from every route that wrote code. If no such route exists, nothing lands.
							</p>
							<p>
								Then Yellowhammer opens <span class="term">one pull request per repository</span>, with the
								per-clause report in the body. A repository with a Blocked Work Card still lands, announced as a
								partial landing. The Act stops at the pull request.
							</p>
						</div>
					</li>

					<li class="stage">
						<p class="mono text-sm c-faint">Morning &middot; 08:00, for example</p>
						<h3 class="mt-1 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance">
							The Night Summary is waiting. You triage.
						</h3>
						<p class="mt-2"><span class="act-label">Night Summary</span></p>
						<div class="mt-4 max-w-[65ch] space-y-3 c-muted">
							<p>
								Every Night closes with a <span class="term">Night Summary</span> on its Night Card in Linear,
								including a Night where nothing was ready. It reports the Night's rates and how close it came to each
								Bound.
							</p>
							<p>
								The board shows what needs you. Each Work Card carries the route that produced it, the checks that
								ran and the number of Rounds. You answer Waiting on You items in Linear, read the Block Reason on
								anything Blocked, and review the pull requests.
							</p>
							<p>
								The verdict comes first, for example:
								<span class="mt-2 block mono c-ink">Night done. 2 pull requests open.</span>
							</p>
						</div>
						<figure class="mt-8 max-w-[65ch]">
							<Image
								src={pulse}
								alt="The Yellowhammer app's Pulse view after a Night. It reads Night done, started 23:37. Nothing needs you. The Feature shows 3 of 3 Cards done with pull request #471 open."
								widths={[640, 960, 1280]}
								sizes="(min-width: 768px) 42rem, calc(100vw - 2rem)"
								format="webp"
								loading="lazy"
								class="h-auto w-full rounded-xl border b-line"
							/>
							<figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm c-faint">
								Pulse, the app's main window, after a Night. Nothing needs you.
							</figcaption>
						</figure>
					</li>
				</ol>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="never-title" class="border-t b-line pt-12 pb-16">
				<h2 id="never-title" class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-balance">What it never does</h2>
				<p class="mt-6 text-2xl font-semibold text-balance sm:text-3xl">
					It never writes a line of code itself.
				</p>
				<p class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold text-balance sm:text-3xl">It never merges to main.</p>
				<p class="mt-6 max-w-[65ch] c-muted">
					The agent CLIs write the code. Yellowhammer judges between them: what to do next, who does it, when to stop
					and what to tell you in the morning. The pull request is where it stops. The merge is the Operator's.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="need-title" class="border-t b-line pt-12 pb-16">
				<h2 id="need-title" class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-balance">What you need</h2>
				<ul class="mt-6 max-w-[65ch] space-y-3">
					<li class="flex gap-3"><span class="c-faint" aria-hidden="true">&mdash;</span>A Mac on macOS 26</li>
					<li class="flex gap-3"><span class="c-faint" aria-hidden="true">&mdash;</span>Orca ADE</li>
					<li class="flex gap-3"><span class="c-faint" aria-hidden="true">&mdash;</span>A Linear workspace</li>
					<li class="flex gap-3"><span class="c-faint" aria-hidden="true">&mdash;</span>GitHub</li>
					<li class="flex gap-3">
						<span class="c-faint" aria-hidden="true">&mdash;</span>At least one supported agent CLI
					</li>
				</ul>
				<p class="mt-6 max-w-[65ch] c-muted">
					Your code, credentials and models stay on your Mac. A Night runs on your existing subscriptions.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="open-title" class="border-t b-line pt-12">
				<h2 id="open-title" class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-balance">Open source</h2>
				<p class="mt-4 max-w-[65ch] c-muted">
					Yellowhammer is open source under the MIT licence. The source is on
					<a href={repo} class="c-ink underline">GitHub</a>.
				</p>
				<div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-4">
					<a href={dmg} class="btn btn-primary">Download for Mac</a>
					<a href={repo} class="btn btn-secondary">Star on GitHub</a>
				</div>
				<p class="mt-4 text-sm c-muted">Requires macOS 26.</p>
			</section>
		</main>

		<footer class="mt-20 flex items-center gap-3 border-t b-line pt-8 text-sm c-muted">
			<img src="/yellowhammer-mark-monochrome-white.svg" alt="" width="24" height="24" class="size-6" />
			<p>&copy; Summer Hammer, LLC</p>
		</footer>
	</div>
</Layout>
